/**
	@help {
		THE GENERAL-PATH METRIC, measured HERMETICALLY.

		Runs the full mizar pipeline on ONE article — regenerated from the Mizar XML every time, so the
		article under test is never inherited from a previous run — and writes every artifact to a
		SCRATCH dir, so the run cannot mutate the golden library under <math>/mizar that its own
		dependencies are read from.

		  russellj no-server=1 test/prover/mizar/general_only article=zfmisc_1        # general path only
		  russellj no-server=1 test/prover/mizar/general_only article=zfmisc_1 off=0  # full stack

		`off=1` (default) disables the hand-written literal-closer battery (no-literal-closers=1), so the
		count reflects ONLY the general machinery: refutation frame, forward saturation, backward bfs, the
		mechanical unfold/setness tables, the congruence closure, the Hilbert emitter. THAT is the number
		that must go UP as the general Mizar decision procedure is built, while the line count of
		src/ru/prover/tactics/literal_closers.flow goes DOWN. The full-stack number (off=0) hides the gap
		— the channels carry it.

		RUN IT THROUGH scripts/test/prover/mizar/measure.sh, NOT DIRECTLY. The pipeline WRITES the proved
		article back into the math library, and the articles form a dependency chain (tarski -> xboole_0 ->
		xboole_1 -> enumset1 -> zfmisc_1), so a run of this script against the REAL library degrades the
		dependencies every later measurement reads — that is how three phantom regressions appeared on
		2026-07-12 (HEAD itself measured zfmisc 126, then 122, then 126). measure.sh gives each run a
		disposable COPY of the library as its math root, so nothing leaks between runs. The generated
		article's output path comes from its module id resolved against import-roots and cannot be
		redirected by a flag — sandboxing the math root is the only clean way.

		The DEPENDENCIES are the golden library, proved with the FULL stack whatever `off` says. That is
		deliberate: `off` says what proves THIS article, not what proved the library it stands on.

		Baseline (2026-07-12, HEAD): general-only tarski 3/3, xboole_0 5/8, xboole_1 111/116,
		enumset1 81/87, zfmisc_1 82/140 = 282/354; full-stack 340/354 (zfmisc_1 126/140).

		Never run two measurements at once: the checker-pipeline stage slices are fixed WALL-CLOCK
		milliseconds, so CPU contention alone loses theorems.
	}
	@defarg article
	@category test

	@arg article { the Mizar article to measure, e.g. zfmisc_1 }
	@arg math    { math root (auto-supplied from $RUSSELL_MATH) }
	@arg off     { 1 = disable the hand-written literal closers (the general-path metric); 0 = full stack @defval 1 }
	@arg tl      { per-step time limit @defval 10s }
	@arg v       { output level @defval 1 }
*/

conf-set no-literal-closers=$off;
translate/mizar/pipeline article=$article math=$math tl=$tl v=$v;
